2026-11-06T16:15:57.0584712Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0585119Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0585624Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0586660Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0587183Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0587574Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0588379Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0589171Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0589939Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0590680Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0591419Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0592318Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0592941Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0593179Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0593482Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0594080Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0594661Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0595166Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0595417Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0595723Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0596041Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0596329Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0596634Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0597015Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0597801Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0598203Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0598511Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0599137Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0599747Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0600345Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0600912Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0601719Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0602859Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0603362Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0603583Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0603891Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0604490Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0605059Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0605562Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0605800Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0606094Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0606401Z 
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0606642Z   ok   _main: --through with a block, or no argument, is a usage error, rc 2
2026-11-06T16:15:57.0607141Z   ok   --through reports the prefix's own failure (null control)
